# Security headers for all pages (Netlify).
# Conservative set — no Content-Security-Policy yet (a strict CSP needs
# report-only testing first so it doesn't break inline scripts, GTM, the
# Cloudflare Turnstile widget, Bunny video embeds, or Google Fonts).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The qualifier is an embeddable widget, so it must be framable. X-Frame-Options
# has no allow-list value, but CSP frame-ancestors takes precedence over it in
# every browser that supports both — so this scopes framing to our own
# properties without weakening the SAMEORIGIN default for the rest of the site.
# Add another origin here if the widget ever goes on a page we don't host.
/qualify/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://jasonmoss.com https://*.jasonmoss.com https://*.netlify.app
